;; spec:   types §2.12, §8.12 (lir.md section 6.1)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   integer rem by zero
;; A division whose divisor is the literal 0 traps like any other
;; (types §2.12), but lIR refuses `srem` by a constant zero outright
;; (lir.md §6.1), so the compiler must emit the trap alone and treat
;; the call as one that does not return, as it treats `trap`. It
;; emitted the guarded `srem` and the module failed lIR's checker
;; (found by `fibc gen`, fibgen seed 239 size 5). The comparison and
;; the branches around the division are never reached.
(defun main () -> i64
  (if (>= (rem 1i32 0i32) 5i32) 6 8))
